@Notes for developers: use `Getlistingstatus to check a list for ID
@Note of Script Writers: USA `SetlistingStatus to change the status of a list in this script
Use: This script brings information to a list when you double -click it. It also has a function that updates a property of a list by modifying that property in the GUI or modifying the value of a variable in a block of text.
Click the right button on any item on the list. Choose "list details" in the menu that appears. The menu will expand and include a list box full of details on the list. You can therefore expand those articles as much as you want to see detailed information. When you start double -clicking something to get more information, you will want a "divided window". Do it at the top left, to the right above the program icon. In this way you can view all the things open in a single screen without having to return to different windows, which is boring.
